## Context
Exit criterion from ticket 0152 (UX audit). The AI persona dry-runs cover
judgment; CI covers the mechanical falsifiable subset that must not regress.

## Three checks to wire

**1. Install steps execute on a clean image**
On every push, a CI job runs the README install sequence verbatim on a fresh
Linux x86-64 image (no pre-installed erg, no tickets/ dir):
```bash
mkdir tickets
curl -fsSL <release-url> -o tickets/erg && chmod +x tickets/erg
tickets/erg init
tickets/erg new "smoke test ticket"
tickets/erg validate tickets/0001-smoke-test-ticket.erg
```
Fails if any step errors or the binary is unreachable.

**2. Time-to-first-ticket budget**
The install sequence above is timed. Fail if wall-clock exceeds budget
(suggested: 60 seconds excluding network). Catches regressions where init
becomes slow or new steps are added to the install path.

**3. Help-completeness regression (from 0068)**
Every `erg COMMAND --help` output is checked to be non-empty and every
command listed in `erg --help` has a corresponding help entry. This already
exists from 0068 — confirm it's wired and not bitrotted.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] CI job runs install sequence verbatim on clean image on every push
- [ ] Time-to-first-ticket measured and gated under a documented budget
- [ ] Help-completeness check confirmed wired (or re-wired if 0068 regressed)
- [ ] All three checks green on main before this ticket closes
